# Repo-root .dockerignore
#
# All four service images build from the REPOSITORY ROOT as their context, not
# from their own subdirectory. That is not a stylistic choice:
# services/{ingestion,verification}/build.rs calls
# tonic_build::compile_protos("../../proto/<svc>.proto"), so proto/ must be
# inside the build context or the Rust builds fail at build-script time.
# One shared context for every image keeps the four Dockerfiles consistent.
#
# The repo is ~3.6MB without build artifacts, so the goal here is correctness
# (never ship a host-built binary or a .env into an image) more than speed.

# --- VCS / tooling ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
**/*.md

# --- secrets: never let a real .env into a layer ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- host build artifacts (would shadow the in-image build) ---
# Only names that actually occur as generated output in this repo are listed.
# Speculative patterns are a hazard here: a blanket `**/build` or `**/dist`
# would silently swallow a future Next.js route directory of the same name and
# the failure would surface as a missing page, not a build error.
**/node_modules
**/target
**/.next
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# --- local state that must never be baked in ---
# NOT `**/reports`: that pattern matched
# apps/web/app/books/[bookId]/reports/, the report-viewer route, and would have
# built a web image with the reports page missing. REPORTS_DIR defaults to
# "reports" relative to the api's CWD, so the real artifact path is this one.
services/api/reports
**/*.log
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup

# --- editor / OS noise ---
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- other apps: not part of any server image ---
apps/mobile

# --- compose files: read by the daemon's client, never needed in an image ---
infra/docker-compose.yml
infra/docker-compose.dev.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
